> Not reached and incomplete together are budget effects: 73--79\% of the gap for the Qwen models, 46\% for DeepSeek-8B and 16--17\% for Phi-mini and Granite-8B. Because greedy forced traces at 512 tokens are prefixes of those at 768, the same trace can be followed as it grows. Take traces that at 512 tokens had written the best option's value as the largest but not finished the list: at 512 the answer picks it in 29--54\%. Among those that finish the list by 768, DeepSeek-8B and the Qwen models then pick it in 84--89\%, but Phi-mini in only 52\% and Granite-8B in 46\%. Unforced traces that finish the list (458--612 per model) agree: the answer passes over the trace's best option in 50\% for Phi-mini and 40\% for Granite-8B against 6--9\% for the other four. For four models the incomplete loss is the budget; for Phi-mini and Granite-8B the decision fails even when the comparison is done. Granite-8B's unforced gap splits 55\% passed over, 27\% arithmetic, 14\% unreached and 4\% incomplete.
